{
  "analysis": "The review describes lives that regenerate over time, creating a wait before another life is available, so T_PlayingByAppointment applies. It also describes daily prizes resetting when a player misses a day, which is an active daily-return incentive with a missed-day penalty, so T_DailyRewards applies. The comments about levels getting harder and small tasks do not specify repetitive actions required for progress, so T_Grinding is rejected; the suggested shorter life timer is not coded as a new mechanic, but the existing regeneration wait remains codable under R12.",
  "labels": [
    {
      "label": "T_PlayingByAppointment",
      "span": "maybe only 5-10 minutes for a new life",
      "rationale": "Describes a time-based life regeneration wait that controls when the player can continue playing."
    },
    {
      "label": "T_DailyRewards",
      "span": "just because you miss a day doesnt mean that you need to start over on your daily prizes",
      "rationale": "Describes daily prizes that reset when the player misses a day, creating a daily-return incentive and penalty."
    }
  ],
  "invoked_web_search": false,
